    "text": "This is a greedy heuristic, not an optimal solver. It places every server it can, so the score is never hurt by a placement, and it tries three server orderings and keeps the best. The program is deterministic and always writes a valid submission, but it carries no optimality guarantee.\n\nEach server goes to the pool with the lowest current guaranteed capacity. Within that pool it goes to the row with the lowest pool load among rows that can fit it. Inside that row it takes the smallest free gap that fits. The worst case is roughly 2\u00b710\u2079 simple operations, so I expect it to fit the 10-second limit, but I have not timed it.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint R, S, U, P, M;\nvector<int> Z, C;\nvector<vector<char>> base;\n\n// Scans a row for free gaps. Returns start of the smallest gap with length >= z\n// (leftmost among ties), or -1 if none. maxg receives the largest gap length.\nint gapScan(const vector<char>& row, int z, int& maxg) {\n    maxg = 0;\n    int bestSt = -1, bestLen = INT_MAX;\n    int n = (int)row.size();\n    int j = 0;\n    while (j < n) {\n        if (row[j]) { j++; continue; }\n        int st = j;\n        while (j < n && !row[j]) j++;\n        int len = j - st;\n        maxg = max(maxg, len);\n        if (len >= z && len < bestLen) {\n            bestLen = len;\n            bestSt = st;\n        }\n    }\n    return bestSt;\n}\n\nstruct Res {\n    long long score;\n    vector<int> ar, as, ap;\n};\n\nRes solveWithOrder(const vector<int>& order) {\n    vector<vector<char>> occ = base;\n    vector<int> maxg(R, 0);\n    for (int r = 0; r < R; r++) {\n        int dummy;\n        gapScan(occ[r], INT_MAX, dummy);\n        maxg[r] = dummy;\n    }\n    vector<long long> L((size_t)P * R, 0), T(P, 0), mx(P, 0), gc(P, 0);\n    set<pair<long long, int>> pq;\n    for (int p = 0; p < P; p++) pq.insert({0LL, p});\n\n    Res res;\n    res.ar.assign(M, -1);\n    res.as.assign(M, -1);\n    res.ap.assign(M, -1);\n\n    for (int idx : order) {\n        int z = Z[idx], c = C[idx];\n        int p = pq.begin()->second;\n        int bestR = -1;\n        long long bestL = LLONG_MAX;\n        for (int r = 0; r < R; r++) {\n            if (maxg[r] >= z) {\n                long long l = L[(size_t)p * R + r];\n                if (l < bestL) {\n                    bestL = l;\n                    bestR = r;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        if (bestR < 0) continue;  // no row can fit this server\n\n        int dummy;\n        int st = gapScan(occ[bestR], z, dummy);\n        if (st < 0) continue;  // should not happen\n        for (int k = st; k < st + z; k++) occ[bestR][k] = 1;\n        {\n            int m;\n            gapScan(occ[bestR], INT_MAX, m);\n            maxg[bestR] = m;\n        }\n\n        pq.erase({gc[p], p});\n        L[(size_t)p * R + bestR] += c;\n        T[p] += c;\n        mx[p] = max(mx[p], L[(size_t)p * R + bestR]);\n        gc[p] = T[p] - mx[p];\n        pq.insert({gc[p], p});\n\n        res.ar[idx] = bestR;\n        res.as[idx] = st;\n        res.ap[idx] = p;\n    }\n    res.score = pq.begin()->first;\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    if (scanf(\"%d %d %d %d %d\", &R, &S, &U, &P, &M) != 5) return 0;\n    base.assign(R, vector<char>(S, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i < U; i++) {\n        int r, s;\n        scanf(\"%d %d\", &r, &s);\n        base[r][s] = 1;\n    }\n    Z.resize(M);\n    C.resize(M);\n    for (int i = 0; i < M; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d %d\", &Z[i], &C[i]);\n    }\n\n    vector<vector<int>> orders;\n\n    // Order 1: capacity descending, then size ascending, then index.\n    {\n        vector<int> idx(M);\n        iota(idx.begin(), idx.end(), 0);\n        sort(idx.begin(), idx.end(), [&](int a, int b) {\n            if (C[a] != C[b]) return C[a] > C[b];\n            if (Z[a] != Z[b]) return Z[a] < Z[b];\n            return a < b;\n        });\n        orders.push_back(idx);\n    }\n    // Order 2: capacity per slot descending.\n    {\n        vector<int> idx(M);\n        iota(idx.begin(), idx.end(), 0);\n        sort(idx.begin(), idx.end(), [&](int a, int b) {\n            long long lhs = (long long)C[a] * Z[b];\n            long long rhs = (long long)C[b] * Z[a];\n            if (lhs != rhs) return lhs > rhs;\n            return a < b;\n        });\n        orders.push_back(idx);\n    }\n    // Order 3: size descending, then capacity descending.\n    {\n        vector<int> idx(M);\n        iota(idx.begin(), idx.end(), 0);\n        sort(idx.begin(), idx.end(), [&](int a, int b) {\n            if (Z[a] != Z[b]) return Z[a] > Z[b];\n            if (C[a] != C[b]) return C[a] > C[b];\n            return a < b;\n        });\n        orders.push_back(idx);\n    }\n\n    Res best;\n    bool have = false;\n    for (auto& ord : orders) {\n        Res r = solveWithOrder(ord);\n        if (!have || r.score > best.score) {\n            best = move(r);\n            have = true;\n        }\n    }\n\n    string out;\n    out.reserve((size_t)M * 16);\n    for (int i = 0; i < M; i++) {\n        if (best.ar[i] < 0) {\n            out += \"x\\n\";\n        } else {\n            out += to_string(best.ar[i]);\n            out += ' ';\n            out += to_string(best.as[i]);\n            out += ' ';\n            out += to_string(best.ap[i]);\n            out += '\\n';\n        }\n    }\n    fputs(out.c_str(), stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
